    {
        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14629\">PR #14629</a> from <code>rvolosatovs:fix/x64-large-callee-pop</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The <code>tail</code> and <code>winch</code> calling conventions pop their stack arguments on return, which x64 does with <code>ret imm16</code>. <code>gen_return</code> converted the size with <code>u16::try_from(..).unwrap()</code>, but stack arguments may be up to 128 MiB, so compiling a <code>tail</code> or <code>winch</code> function with 64 KiB or more of stack arguments, or a <code>tail</code> function that <code>return_call</code>s such a callee, panicked.</p>\n<p>Reject such signatures with <code>CodegenError::ImplLimitExceeded</code> in <code>compute_arg_locs</code>, alongside the existing stack-argument size limit. Since this runs for every signature a function references, it also covers the callee's signature at <code>return_call</code> sites, which grows the caller's tail-argument area. Other backends pop with an <code>sp</code> adjustment and aren't affected. Wasm can't reach this: 1000 parameters is about 16 KiB of stack arguments.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630483568,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791565843
    },
